        },
        {
          "block_id": "b00129",
          "quote": "RF-EMR (0.15 W/kg) to determine its ability to impair DNA integrity. These spermatozoa were subsequently assessed for DNA damage using the (A) alkaline comet assay (B) and halo assay. (C) From cells exposed for 4 h, DNA was extracted via the use of phenol-chloroform and analyzed for the presence of oxidative DNA damage utilizing an 8-OHdG ELISA. *p < 0.05 compared to unexposed controls."
        },
        {
          "block_id": "b00134",
          "quote": "RF-EMR alters sperm motility but not tail tyrosine phosphorylation levels. Mature mouse spermatozoa isolated from the cauda epididymis were exposed to RF-EMR of an intensity of 0.15 W/kg for periods of up to 4 h."
        },
